# Description: Select the master file (MF), the root directory of the card.
# Category: selection
#
# WHAT THIS DOES
# Every smart card with a file system has one "master file" (MF), which is
# the root folder of everything stored on the card. Selecting it is a safe,
# standard operation: nothing on the card is modified. Afterwards the MF is
# the "currently selected file", which is where many other commands (such
# as READ BINARY) act.
#
# THE COMMAND, BYTE BY BYTE
#   00     class byte: standard interindustry commands
#   A4     instruction: SELECT FILE
#   00     P1 = 0: select by file identifier, first occurrence
#   00     P2 = 0: first or only occurrence, no control info requested
#   02     Lc: exactly 2 data bytes follow
#   3F 00  file identifier reserved for the MF by the ISO 7816-4 standard
#
# WHAT YOU SHOULD SEE
#   SW 90 00          the MF was selected (success)
#   SW 61 XX          success, plus XX bytes of file-control data waiting;
#                     fetch them afterwards with the get_response script
#   other SW          the card may have no MF at all (for example an
#                     application-only card without a file system)
#
# This command does not write anything to the card.
00 A4 00 00 02 3F 00
